            "properties": {
                "0": {
                    "name": "block",
                    "value": "Picks indices at random, each as likely as its probability: with 0.125 0.125 0.25 0.5, index 3 comes up half the time and index 0 one time in eight.\n\nIt is how a trained network that predicts \"what comes next\" is played. Such a network (t.model) ends with a score for every possible next note, word, gesture or pose;\nt.nn.softmax turns the scores into probabilities, and t.multinomial picks one - the likely choices most of the time, the unlikely ones now and then, so the result is neither fixed nor arbitrary. Feed each choice back in, and the network writes a sequence. Without a network it is weighted chance: a pose to move to, a clip, a direction, each as often as you choose.\n\nThe probabilities need not add up to 1 - 1 1 2 4 means the same as the list above - but none may be negative and not all may be 0. Give one row per distribution (a 2-D tensor) and each row gets its own pick, in one step. The picks are made on the probabilities' device.\n\nSYNTAX:\nt.multinomial <count>\nDefault: count 1.\n\nINPUTS and PARAMETERS:\n\nprobabilities:\nHow likely each index is: a list or tensor, or one row per distribution. Every input picks and sends.\n\ncount (int box, also an inlet):\nHow many to pick. 1 (the default) sends the index itself (one per row for rows); more sends them as a list.\n\ntemperature (float box, also an inlet):\nReshapes the probabilities before the pick: each is raised to the power 1/temperature. 1 (the default) leaves them as they are. Below 1 the likely choices grow likelier - near 0 the most likely is chosen almost every time. Above 1 the choices even out - the music grows more surprising. It is the main control for playing a generative model.\n\nrepeats:\nAn option, under the node. On (the default), an index can be picked again within one count. Off, each at most once per count - like dealing cards (count is then at most the number of choices).\n\nseed:\nAn option, under the node. -1 (the default) draws different numbers every time the patch opens. Any other number starts the same sequence every time - the same \"random\" piece on every run, which is what you want for rehearsal, comparison and debugging.\n\nOUTPUTS:\n\nchosen:\nThe index picked, or the list of indices.\n\nREADING THE DEMO:\nTop: 16 picks from 0 1 2 3 with probabilities 0.125 0.125 0.25 0.5, twice a second:\nabout eight 3s, four 2s, and two each of 0 and 1 - different every time.\n\nBottom: a model's scores for four notes, 0 1 2 3, made into probabilities by t.nn.softmax (0.03 0.09 0.24 0.64), and one note picked from them. Drag temperature down towards 0.1 and the top note takes over; up towards 5 and all four come up almost equally.\n\nRELATED:\nnp.random.choice picks from a list of items. t.nn.softmax turns scores into probabilities; t.model runs the network that makes the scores. t.argmax always takes the most likely, with no chance at all.",
                    "value_type": "str"
                },
                "1": {
                    "name": "lock",
                    "value": true,
                    "value_type": "bool"
                },
                "2": {
                    "name": "width",
                    "value": 760,
